        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Gives plugins the ability to specify the atomicity of their actions.\r\n\r\nNo longer necessary, because `CmdAtom` figures out the atomicity automatically, without plugin coordination/participation. (https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41415 tracks potential ability for plugins to \"annotate\" user actions, but is a last resort.)\r\n\r\n> Does this new feature do at least the `.` enhancement automatically?\r\n\r\nNot yet, and probably won't do that until we are confident. You just need the autocmd + mapping given at `:help edit-repeat`: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/887541161392ea75dee5c03e39acef6a2f98f5b7/runtime/doc/repeat.txt#L100-L103\r\n\r\nAnd uninstall vim-repeat so that it doesn't try to define its own \".\" mapping.",
